    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>According to question meter bridge have non-uniform wire, where its resistance has a variation with length as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>l</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#8733;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>l</mi></msqrt></mfrac></math>&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>l</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>k</mi><msqrt><mi>l</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>, where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math>&nbsp;is proportionality constant<br />Let resistance of the left part&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;and right part <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;of the wire is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub></math>&nbsp;respectively.</p><p>From balanced condition of wheat stone bridge is:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi></mfrac></math></p><p>So, from the above condition for given meter bridge is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>'</mo></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Now from equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math>, on integrating&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8747;</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>&#8747;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>l</mi></mrow><msqrt><mi>l</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>&nbsp;for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;part of the wire of length extends from&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>o</mi></math>&nbsp;to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi></math>&nbsp;from the equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub></msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>l</mi></mrow><msqrt><mi>l</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><msup><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></msup></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><msup><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mfenced><mn>0</mn><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi><msqrt><mi>l</mi></msqrt></math></p><p>Now, for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;part of the wire of length extends from&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi></math>&nbsp;to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>m</mi></math>, from the equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub></msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>l</mi></mrow><msqrt><mi>l</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><msup><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></msup></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><msup><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mfenced><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mi>l</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;</p><p>From equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mi>l</mi></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mi>l</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfenced><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msqrt><mi>l</mi></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mi>l</mi></msqrt><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><msqrt><mi>l</mi></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>m</mi></math></p>"
  }
